    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d766">

                <pb facs="0788" n="530" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg530"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 841.857Ar1/48</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-31T13:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 31, 1915, 1 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received September 1, 12.38 p.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2809. I believe that German Government is anxious that <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Arabic</hi> case should not have <hi rendition="#italic">Lusitania</hi>
                    case brought in with it. It is easier for the Government to base its concessions
                    on <hi rendition="#italic">Arabic</hi> case because <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Arabic</hi> was going west and carried no ammunition. Popular feeling has
                    been worked on because of Von Tirpitz
                    party making the situation difficult for Chancellor. Above information given me
                    by friend who has many acquaintances in Reichstag, not in any way from
                    Government.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
